---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';import{currentData}from'../lib/data';const{index}=await currentData();
const limits = (key: 'max_tokens' | 'thinking_tokens' | 'agent_steps') => {
  const values = [...new Set(index.conditions.map(condition => condition[key]))];
  const recorded = values.filter((value): value is number => typeof value === 'number').sort((a, b) => a - b);
  const labels = recorded.map(value => value.toLocaleString('en-US'));
  if (values.some(value => value == null) || values.length === 0) labels.push('Unrecorded');
  return labels.join(' / ');
};
---
<Shell title="How to read the results"><div class="eyebrow">Methodology & limitations</div><h1>Useful evidence.<br/>Clear boundaries.</h1><p class="lede">These results describe a finite set of text-only tasks on specific local configurations. They are intended to help you choose what to investigate and to make every reported result inspectable.</p><div class="two-column"><div><section class="panel"><h2>Scores and coverage</h2><p>Each configuration retains its predetermined question set. The observed score averages only assessed answers. A perfect average on a partial run remains a preview, not a complete result.</p><p>Blocked, infrastructure-error, context-limit and review outcomes remain visible without invented zero scores. A measured zero means an answer received no credit. Repeated attempts and corrected grades stay in the history; only the canonical outcome contributes to a baseline score.</p><p>Binary suites show passed/scored counts. Other suites report mean credit or F1; those are not pass percentages. Capability groups are navigation labels, with no combined overall ranking.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Thinking and repeated trials</h2><p>Thinking controls are checked with saved profile-level probes. “Requested off” does not establish an absence of reasoning. Historical probe scope may not identify every exact template/runtime build.</p><p>Thinking comparisons match question versions, seed, sampling, artifact and execution configuration. Score pairs and valid positive-duration time pairs have separate counts. Incomplete pairs are previews. Basic-task sampled seeds remain separate from the greedy baseline.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Time, file size and memory</h2><p>Benchmark task time includes applicable tools, setup and grading. Model loading is separate. Timings describe this machine and the recorded setup; runtime and offload changes are not isolated quantization experiments.</p><p>Parameter categories use total parameters, with separate dense and MoE groups. When derived from GGUF headers, counts describe stored tensor elements; active/effective counts remain separately attributed. Category boundaries are versioned and the roster can grow.</p><p>Memory filters use decimal GB budgets for exact quants and runtime profiles. Verified fit requires documented measurements and system headroom; estimates are labeled and unknown requirements remain unclassified. System RAM, GPU VRAM, and unified memory are separate choices. Smaller supported tiers are included in larger budget filters.</p><p>Download-size groups use decimal gigabytes of all recorded weight shards. They do not imply a RAM requirement. Process RSS, device-wide VRAM and system available RAM measure different things and are never added together.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Exact evidence and availability</h2><p>Original final answers, references, captured input envelopes, tool results and reasoning are shown where recorded and permitted. Model-generated code is displayed as inert text. The site does not execute answers.</p><p>Components are labeled full, redacted, source-link-only, not recorded or withheld. Named privacy rules replace private host paths; redacted content is visibly marked. Starting workspace snapshots may be unavailable even when tool change records survive.</p><p>Full QASPER papers link to their sources until redistribution is established per paper. The question and accepted answer annotations retain dataset attribution. External live filesystem artifacts require per-item publication review.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Analyst summaries</h2><p>The configured analyst is GPT Astra, model ID <code>gpt-6-astra</code>. Generated summaries require evidence citations, numeric validation and human review. Each approved summary will retain its own requested and returned model IDs, prompt/evidence versions, generation date and editorial history.</p><p>Changing the configured analyst cannot relabel older summaries. Factual fallback text does not receive an Astra authorship badge. Current pages explicitly identify analysis that has not yet been generated.</p></section></div><aside><section class="card"><h3>Recorded experiment limits</h3><p>{limits('max_tokens')} completion tokens, including thinking</p><p>{limits('thinking_tokens')} requested thinking-token cap</p><p>{limits('agent_steps')} agent steps</p><p>All recorded values are listed; limits can differ between configurations. <a href="/models/">Inspect each model’s setup</a> for its limits, requested context and observed placement.</p><small>Exact historical hardware names were not fully captured in the public source metadata. Do not extrapolate task times to other machines.</small></section><section class="card" style="margin-top:20px"><h3 id="summary-limitations">Interpretation limits</h3><p>Small convenience-selected subsets, known public questions, correlated repeats and some live tasks limit generalization.</p><p>These suites do not establish broad creative-writing, multimodal, long-context or general open-ended ability.</p><a href="/tests/">Inspect all test definitions →</a></section></aside></div><section class="panel"><h2>Sources and terms</h2>{index.suites.map(s=><p><strong>{s.name}.</strong> {s.source.attribution} {s.source.terms_url&&<a href={s.source.terms_url}>Terms</a>}</p>)}</section></Shell>
